# Sulci Cache — Context-Aware Semantic LLM Cache

Sulci Cache is a LlamaIndex-compatible LLM cache that adds context-aware semantic lookup — blending prior conversation turns into the similarity vector at query time, rather than matching the current prompt in isolation.

This targets the multi-turn ambiguity problem: a follow-up like "What are the main differences?" is semantically ambiguous without conversation history. A stateless cache matches it against everything; Sulci Cache anchors it to the recent turns in the session.
If you're opening this Notebook on Colab, you will probably need to install LlamaIndex 🦙.
